in used to borrow the best performing architectures or structures and try to modify a little bit to work for their problem. And they try to tweak some of the features of the structure and compare these different tweaks. And then they say that we found the best performing structure.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.983336329460144, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.19143947958946228, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.10538756102323532, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.018093645572662354, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0046618045307695866, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008449265151284635, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0007468117401003838, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0005941700655966997, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0005246434011496603, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0005019239033572376, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 153970, 'end': 196726}, 'sentences_idx_start': 20, 'sentences_idx_end': 23}, {'text': "But to actually find an absolute optimum structure concerning that solution, it would be an NP hard problem because to reach that solution, they had to try all the combinations of the different structural elements, right? Because we have massive structures in these deep neural networks, it could be an NPR problem because we don't have computational power or enough time to actually train and test all these structures, all these structures constructed from these different combinations of structure elements.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7034947872161865, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003050185739994049, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0025971480645239353, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002067766385152936, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.000660270918160677, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00033956501283682883, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0002290900010848418, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00019151638844050467, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00018549474771134555, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.000182950752787292, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 196838, 'end': 242454}, 'sentences_idx_start': 24, 'sentences_idx_end': 25}, {'text': "So the alternative way to do this is to actually try to apply a meteoristic method to convert to a near to upper solution that is much better than not optimizing the structure or relying on kind of like a random search, right? A random search can get us better performing neural network, but it's not going to give us a near to optimal solution or to converge to a near to optimal solution.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9319981932640076, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0007628374733030796, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>PolarTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.000679380726069212, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00033721968065947294, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.000268077157670632, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00023321257322095335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00015840237028896809, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.00015099153097253293, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00014779010962229222, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>TalkRadio>BusinessNewsRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.0001474309101467952, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoParts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 242582, 'end': 270610}, 'sentences_idx_start': 26, 'sentences_idx_end': 27}, {'text': 'So a minoristic method would give us an automated method and also would converge to optimum structure new to optimum solution to this structure problem. So the way that people approached Nas was by trying to mimic how optimization is done in nature, right? So the first way they thought of it was trying to mimic how living organisms evolve in nature using genetic based algorithm like the Darwinian Genetic Evolution.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.36338284611701965, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.010852179490029812, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.008103647269308567, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.007776046637445688, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.004191715270280838, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0013245012378320098, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00020261337340343744, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00018652893777471036, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00018463908054400235, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00013606487482320517, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 274630, 'end': 319090}, 'sentences_idx_start': 28, 'sentences_idx_end': 30}, {'text': "It started with Neat, it's a short for Neuralution of Augmenting topologies and it relied on genetic algorithms where also that concept also applied in most of the Nas and Neural evolution methods and Exam is one of them. Travis came up with this method and it became one of the state of the art methods in Nas.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.40113142132759094, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance'