ocation and then decides if it's going to do an exploitation or if the next move will be exploitation or exploration move. And this example will be an exploitation move. So it will try to exploit the pheromone traces, the hormone that was previously deposited by other ants in the search space.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7112300395965576, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0025254052598029375, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0005634177359752357, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.000551211298443377, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.00045459732064045966, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.00028678763192147017, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00026923647965304554, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00025707995519042015, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00022272109345067292, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00020864701946265996, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2543806, 'end': 2582958}, 'sentences_idx_start': 228, 'sentences_idx_end': 232}, {'text': "So it will use its sensing radius, that's something that is previously defined for each ant. And then it will find the center of mass of the hormone traces. And then when it calculates that center of mass of the hormone, it will consider it as its next location and then it will move to that spot. And then it will decide about if its next move will be an exploitation exploration move at each location before it's deciding about the type of the step.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5563836693763733, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0011271234834566712, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0010863780044019222, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.000977685209363699, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0005333833978511393, 'label': 'Techno