elevance': 0.0003070567036047578, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>Agriculture'}, {'relevance': 0.00030565328779630363, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00026696384884417057, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3500650, 'end': 3545762}, 'sentences_idx_start': 299, 'sentences_idx_end': 303}, {'text': "They interact with other colonies, and they die at some point. And the ants themselves are not organisms. They are the cells of these organisms, this colony organisms. So we want to take that concept and apply it in our methods to have number of colonies living together in parallel, evolving and communicating with each other. And we want to see if this would give us a better performance, because, after all, we're trying to mimic nature in the solutions we're trying to investigate.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8886245489120483, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.008666090667247772, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0028008457738906145, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0023108378518372774, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.001042830990627408, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0008512925123795867, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005421679234132171, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.00048124196473509073, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.00028928855317644775, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028792733792215586, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3545826, 'end': 3581730}, 'sentences_idx_start': 304, 'sentences_idx_end': 308}, {'text': "So with this, I'm done with my presentation, and if you have any questions all right. Awesome. Wow, what a great presentation. How about Travis and Alexander? Either of you which want to go first, please feel free to give an introduction and any primary remarks that you have on that. Okay. I can say something. I don't have too much to add. I think Abdul Rahman did a pretty good job going over the core bits of the work. I'm Alex Rorbia.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.044540926814079285, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.03510531783103943, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.02202454023063183, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.020386802032589912, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.018277321010828018, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.00933101400732994, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.007808041293174028, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.007780127692967653, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.005281268619000912, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.004898932296782732, 'label': 'Education>CollegeEducation>PostgraduateEducation>ProfessionalSchool'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3584470, 'end': 3627024}, 'sentences_idx_start': 309, 'sentences_idx_end': 318}, {'text': "I'm an assistant professor in computer science, an affiliate professor in psychology, and affiliate faculty in computational neuroscience at the Rochester Institute of Technology. And I work on a lot of stuff, but primarily predictive coding, active inference variational, free energy, a lot of the stuff that's actually of interest to this. Yeah, and this was a particularly interesting project for me because a branch of my own research is working in neurovolutionary methods or even just nature inspired metahuristic optimization.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6530263423919678, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.024981748312711716, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.015818458050489426, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.006891054101288319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005102593917399645, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0044778333976864815, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0024983566254377365, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0009151170961558819, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006308059673756361, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005575037212111056, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3627152, 'end': 3662320}, 'sentences_idx_start': 319, 'sentences_idx_end': 321}, {'text': "And when I got the pleasure of working with Abdul Rahman when he was a PhD student at Know, we talked a lot about the ant colony based optimization approaches, and I encouraged him to look into sort of, like, the origins and also try to understand actually how physical ants behave. So that was always fascinating to me. I don't have too much to add in terms of the technical parts. I think he covered all the core results. The only thing I like to think about.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9599403738975525, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0017083153361454606, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.000584155903197825, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0005435833591036499, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002798131899908185, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.0002795390610117465, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0002708153915591538, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.00024394142383243889, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AutomotiveIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002273318823426962, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.00021625973749905825, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3662660, 'end': 3693112}, 'sentences_idx_start': 322, 'sentences_idx_end': 326}, {'text': "And I'm actually more fascinated, too, to hear from the active inference institute their interest in the ant colony methods and particularly what was interesting to them. Because thinking about what does ant colony optimization how do you view it from an active inference perspective is, I think, particularly interesting and thinking. And I even had a thought, I don't know if this was a question among the audience's mind.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.501878559589386, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0026314749848097563, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001965336501598358, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0014618461718782783, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.001135926111601293, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0009206091635860503, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009147143573500216, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0008376121404580772, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.0008056673686951399, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0006178881740197539, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3693166, 'end': 3719504}, 'sentences_idx_start': 327, 'sentences_idx_end': 329}, {'text': "Do the little ant agents or the cant agents that run and described what is there a way to start to view them as a multi agent system that's optimizing some variational free energy quantity? Because a lot of even Carl's work I mean, I collaborate with him, sort of touches into this area of, like, well, what happens with collective intelligence and societal organization? And you can kind of look at free energy from these very high level viewpoints all the way down to fine grained cellular activity.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.33331453800201416, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.08257807046175003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.01164349727332592, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.009511127136647701, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00911212619394064, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.005258352495729923, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020963726565241814, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.002029055031016469, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0019283252768218517, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.001102209440432489, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3719702, 'end': 3754264}, 'sentences_idx_start': 330, 'sentences_idx_end': 332}, {'text': "And so I'm actually more curious to know Daniel and anyone else in the active inferences who can sort of explain their particular interest in ant based optimization and meta heuristic optimization. I'm curious to know that. But there could be some interesting viewpoints, like, what is the free energy? I think the ants themselves are very mean. We have made them more intelligent.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.379954069852829, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0010313679231330752, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007310033543035388, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006641143118031323, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0004427376843523234, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.000433931068982929, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0003435625694692135, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00023791617422830313, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00022244179854169488, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.0002179843868361786, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3754312, 'end': 3777936}, 'sentences_idx_start': 333, 'sentences_idx_end': 337}, {'text': 'I know Abdul Raman and I talked at length about, well, what if we even made them, for example, have, like, a reinforcement learning control system? And you could even imagine, well, now, what if the cans themselves engage in a form of active inference themselves? What would that look like for the system? And they are optimizing their own free energy. Those are just fun little thought experiments. We have obviously not worked on them.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9008342027664185, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.7815684080123901, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.013279403559863567, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.005309350788593292, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>RadioControl'}, {'relevance': 0.0035759585443884134, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0031675505451858044, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0015525645576417446, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001426692702807486, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.0012548029189929366, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.001240540761500597, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3777968, 'end': 3803692}, 'sentences_idx_start': 338, 'sentences_idx_end': 343}, {'text': "At least Abdul Rahman was never exposed by me to that part of my world and biomimetic intelligence. So those are my comments. I'm not sure if they're particularly helpful, but they're very general, and I'm actually more curious to know from the active inference institute, their interest in it and where does that maybe perhaps intersect? Or this is just like, oh, we know interesting topics and yeah. Thank you. Alexander.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9970587491989136, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.06631951034069061, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.011919351294636726, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003888176055625081, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0020667649805545807, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0007540129008702934, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005943867145106196, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0005413228645920753, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0005399382789619267, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0004873732686974108, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3803826, 'end': 3833840}, 'sentences_idx_start': 344, 'sentences_idx_end': 349}, {'text': "Travis, you want to say hello and give any reflections on the talk? Sure, I'll come in. Hopefully you can see me a little bit. My jungle here. Hi, I'm Travis is Sell. I'm an associate professor at RIT. I'm also the graduate program director for a master's in data science. So if any of you are interested in any of this or data science, please shoot me an email.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6383060812950134, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.02215777523815632, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0011714330175891519, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009798243409022689, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.000621215789578855, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0004537286004051566, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0004323525936342776, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00040451946551911533, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0003866824263241142, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0003021250886376947, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3834000, 'end': 3856110}, 'sentences_idx_start': 350, 'sentences_idx_end': 357}, {'text': "No, I thought this work was really very interesting in a lot of ways while Abdul Rahman was working on it. I think one of the coolest parts about it is a popular neuroevolution algorithm that came after neat is called hyperneet, and it transforms the discrete search space of neural architecture search into a continuous one. And it's shown to be a pretty powerful method. Well, this version of ant colony optimization, the new one, does the same thing. It makes the search space continuous.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12228882312774658, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.008910179138183594, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005458630155771971, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0019498547771945596, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006051017553545535, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0005399858928285539, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005076711531728506, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0003657076449599117, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.00033676234306767583, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0002954231749754399, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3857200, 'end': 3889284}, 'sentences_idx_start': 358, 'sentences_idx_end': 362}, {'text': "But what I found was really cool about it was that as opposed to traditional ant colony optimization where you have a graph and you just send the ants along the edges of the graph and you take the best paths and construct a graph after it. Here the ants are actually working like ants in the real world where they'll move a continuous amount of space, not just from point A to point B and actually dropping down pheromones.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7665849924087524, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.00034751073690131307, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.00021575368009507656, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00017223555187229067, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0001508467539679259, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00014589638158213347, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00014438192010857165, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0001321137824561447, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00012423720909282565, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>Agriculture'}, {'relevance': 0.00012180049088783562, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>FoodIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3889332, 'end': 3913436}, 'sentences_idx_start': 363, 'sentences_idx_end': 364}, {'text': "And it's more like a real simulation of how ants would move around in the real world. And we're getting better results from it than some of the older methods. So I think that really made me kind of happy to see that and thought it made it as very interesting work. That's awesome. Ahmed, want to add anything or I'm happy to give a thought on the answer and ask some questions from the live chat. I'm good.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9040632843971252, 'label': '