eping'}, {'relevance': 0.003233681432902813, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0020128751639276743, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0017184255411848426, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007964411634020507, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.00034793574013747275, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.00027177215088158846, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.00023416595649905503, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.00020853742898907512, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.00020718456653412431, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4344398, 'end': 4369504}, 'sentences_idx_start': 413, 'sentences_idx_end': 419}, {'text': "And the idea is it's saying, well, OK, I want to understand my world. And the more that I explore my world, right, there will be things that surprise me less. But if I encounter some information that is really weird when I build a generative world model or a predictive world model, that's very surprising, I should probably explore that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1326437145471573, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.025158608332276344, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0024846026208251715, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001329394057393074, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001203093328513205, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0011572432704269886, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0011403847020119429, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010531161678954959, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009591366979293525, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.000936815922614187, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4369542, 'end': 4391256}, 'sentences_idx_start': 420, 'sentences_idx_end': 422}, {'text': "And so, of course, I'm condensing the concept down into sort of like the exploration part of the explore exploit trade off that I know, you know, but that characterizes reinforcement learning. So that's just what we mean when we say epistemic or epistemic foraging. And obviously, Abdul Rahman foraging can be likened to what the ants are doing, right? They're exploring their environment. And so I guess with that in mind.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.030952313914895058, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0025130240246653557, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0017325024819001555, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0006324189016595483, 'label': 'Sports>FishingSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0006006265175528824, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.0005394506151787937, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.000401042663725093, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}, {'relevance': 0.00035083122202195227, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0003246208652853966, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00029359612381085753, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4391438, 'end': 4416592}, 'sentences_idx_start': 423, 'sentences_idx_end': 427}, {'text': "So that way everyone's sort of on the same page here to get to your question about the differences, about how does this work versus your typical neural based approaches to active inference. And I would fall into that category of, oh, I build neural models, biological process models. Those are very much focused, you could say, at the individual level, at least the ones that I am aware of.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.4020639657974243, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.029009554535150528, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.006229750346392393, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.003961899783462286, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002801185240969062, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002533498452976346, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0022600041702389717, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012051360681653023, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006838717963546515, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.00044109270675107837, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4416646, 'end': 4439096}, 'sentences_idx_start': 428, 'sentences_idx_end': 430}, {'text': "When you're building, for example, even a back propagation based, partially observable Markov decision process in active inference, that's like a single agent, right? You're trying to build this construct that is trying to balance the epistemic quantity with its instrumental term, which, by the way, another jargon term for you, Abdul Rahman and Travis, that's just like your reward signal or your prior preference or a prior distribution over goal states.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06180308014154434, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.006019937340170145, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0010305381147190928, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0009850106434896588, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0008479603566229343, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0006472905515693128, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.000615039374679327, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005026768194511533, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00044691114453598857, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.000441443087765947, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4439118, 'end': 4467232}, 'sentences_idx_start': 431, 'sentences_idx_end': 432}, {'text': "And so these agents sort of like deal with that trade off, but at an individual agent level. Now, again, I'm sure that there's interpretations of these from other perspectives, the ant based approach, even though I would not argue per se that this has at least an explicit form or a connection, at least that Abdul Rahman has made clear to active inference. But the idea is that this is like a multi agent approach to active inference.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09881311655044556, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0018079678993672132, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015844580484554172, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.0013172765029594302, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0008912014309316874, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0007354130502790213, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0005561821744777262, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0005137738189660013, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0004954268806613982, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0004871953569818288, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4467366, 'end': 4493172}, 'sentences_idx_start': 433, 'sentences_idx_end': 435}, {'text': "And so the ants, when they conduct their epistemic foraging, which arguably is a very simple model, each ant and of themselves is essentially a bunch of coefficients and some hard coded rules because their job is essentially to work together with their pheromone trails to figure out oh, what parts of the superstructure are useful. So I'd say that that's different and it lends itself in some ways.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5986308455467224, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.003848043503239751, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0013654440408572555, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0012645544484257698, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.001094473642297089, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00030117834103293717, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00024766838760115206, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.000240049121202901, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.00023566819436382502, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002251115656690672, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4493236, 'end': 4521040}, 'sentences_idx_start': 436, 'sentences_idx_end': 437}, {'text': "Of course, you can make the ants more complicated and lose the benefit of I'm just about to say you could massively paralyze this. And this is one of the key strengths that I think is natural. In, for example, a lot of actually nature inspired optimization algorithms and ant colony optimization is one of them.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6366550922393799, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.001285318285226822, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007909144624136388, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.00047052156878635287, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00043708080193027854, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00031450032838620245, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.00020105400471948087, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00018934677063953131, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.00016133490134961903, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>Agriculture'}, {'relevance': 0.00014856581401545554, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4521110, 'end': 4539416}, 'sentences_idx_start': 438, 'sentences_idx_end': 440}, {'text': "Is Abdul Rahman has been using hundreds of CPUs, and you can put these ants on their own individual processor, and the communication that's occurring across them as they exchange information is through the pheromone trails. There's an indirect mechanism, it's not terribly complex to facilitate. And I'm sure that there's even better ways to go about doing asynchronous forms of communication and further, further optimize this.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08692950755357742, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.010250692255795002, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00823997426778078, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.005510345101356506, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0031643961556255817, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0018713099416345358, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0016044864896684885, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.001495738630183041, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012926949420943856, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0010533679742366076, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Laptops'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4539438, 'end': 4564944}, 'sentences_idx_start': 441, 'sentences_idx_end': 443}, {'text': 'I know Travis and Travis can add to this has done things on like, citizen science and distributed computing through volunteer computing and how you can distribute this through a massive global Asynchronous network. So you can imagine adapting the ant form sorry, the ant colony optimization approach to some distributed, massively distributed version of active inference, where you essentially have to write down that the variational free energy.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5525302290916443, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.11050369590520859, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.006529956124722958, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0034290810581296682, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0033812671899795532, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0031223571859300137, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0022762224543839693, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0017853624885901809, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0010797029826790094, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009590380941517651, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4564982, 'end': 4594440}, 'sentences_idx_start': 444, 'sentences_idx_end': 445}, {'text': "And I'm putting quotes around this because, again, there is no concrete term written in Raman's work because at least we haven't viewed this from the active inference perspective directly. Each ant is optimizing its own variational free energy, but then there's probably a global quantity that sort of is related as a function of those pheromone trails in the individual ant agents.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3043077290058136, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.003026046324521303, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00115979800466