ul just by itself with or without reliance on some other electronic phenomena.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9263924956321716, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0545756034553051, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.012403962202370167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.010043949820101261, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004407323431223631, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0023680292069911957, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.001717972569167614, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0012563593918457627, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007004120270721614, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005687658558599651, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4741054, 'end': 4783300}, 'sentences_idx_start': 460, 'sentences_idx_end': 461}, {'text': "So it's just a lot of very interesting connections like having the degrees of freedom on the blanket which could be noiseless and four bits or it could be noisy with this really specific thing. But in Silico you get to play it from both sides and scale things up and down and do these meta heuristics on top of that arbitrary space could be really simple for learning, or it could be however much.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0326809398829937, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.029388323426246643, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.020017247647047043, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>AudioProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.009597751311957836, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.008144225925207138, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.007797439582645893, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.0072