r both niche modification and behavioral and cognitive modeling. So just to add on because I think and then also what the node is could even be heterogeneous or unknown or fit in different ways or fix through design processes.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2729400396347046, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.018606314435601234, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.013203170150518417, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.004233259242027998, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0019152044551447034, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0011606861371546984, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0008846459095366299, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0007256430108100176, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007040677010081708, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0006391999777406454, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4840380, 'end': 4864364}, 'sentences_idx_start': 467, 'sentences_idx_end': 468}, {'text': "So just like the ant colonies are flexible, enabling them to live in all kinds of places, make all these kinds of nested decisions that interact with each other, that flexibility is just like the tip of the iceberg, of what we could even just describe, because there would always be real environments we hadn't yet tried with ant colonies. So we really would never know the full extent of all the repertoire and the dynamics of the ant system.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6094903349876404, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0038752492982894182, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0018700502114370465, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0009467247873544693, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007353923283517361, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'rele