 certain way or there really are only this many pheromones do model comparison. So it's a lot of degrees of freedom. I feel like you all are opening up with the ant collie modeling. And also one of the challenging pieces of multi agent simulation is kind of like the open endedness with the design space.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08830711990594864, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.02054859884083271, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.016985485330224037, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.015320396982133389, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0019984827376902103, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0017775713931769133, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0008583115413784981, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007391758845187724, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.000652743095997721, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005747544346377254, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4926250, 'end': 4951790}, 'sentences_idx_start': 476, 'sentences_idx_end': 479}, {'text': "So then it's very hard for even creative ideas like sometimes to find the right compute resources that obviously are still even needed for what he discovered with the analysis. Here I'll ask a question from Bert in the to before we move on to that, I just want to clarify just so make sure that I got the right term and certainly Abdul Rahman and Travis might want to look it up is when you were saying blanket, you were referring to a Markov blanket, correct? Yes.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03473540395498276, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.005418643821030855, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.004144273232668638, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.001836354611441493, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0006952871335670352, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0004174954374320805, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Desktops'}, {'relevance': 0.00039454366196878254, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0003617270849645138, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00035450782161206007, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00029916365747340024, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4952960, 'end': 4982356}, 'sentences_idx_start': 480, 'sentences_idx_end': 482}, {'text': "So the technical definition of Markov blanket is when you have a Bayesian graph where nodes are the variables and edges are relationships amongst these variables. For any given node of interest, we'll just call it internal states. So these are not features of the world. It's not tagged onto some tissue of a real nest mate in the world.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.008132985793054104, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0017658500000834465, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011147058103233576, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0007998811779543757, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006103715277276933, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0003578616597224027, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028125749668106437, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00022602129320148379, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.00020208318892400712, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00016654396313242614, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4982458, 'end': 5000056}, 'sentences_idx_start': 483, 'sentences_idx_end': 486}, {'text': "This is something that's tagged onto or like a perspective we could take on any node in a Bayes graph and then all the nodes that insulate it and the co parents are known as the blanket in the sense that it's like one layer insulator. And there's a lot of more discussion on it and the philosophical implications and all these generalizations of that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.009878704324364662, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.004347851034253836, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.002945082960650325, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00032809749245643616, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00027584712370298803, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.00023086657165549695, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00017637004202697426, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00016390781092923135, 'label': 'Home&Garden>IndoorEnvironmentalQuality'}, {'relevance': 0.0001301198935834691, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00012195123417768627, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5000158, 'end': 5020770}, 'sentences_idx_start': 487, 'sentences_idx_end': 488}, {'text': "But broadly, the Markov blanket is just the inbound dependencies which we associate with sense making and perception learning attention and then the outgoing dependencies for the agent which we associate with action influence in some downstream pointing way. Thank you. I just wanted to clarify that because I don't think Abdul Rahman and Travis might be familiar just with that terminology. It's very know, very active inferency kind of jargon. So I wanted to make sure that they got that from the physics point of thanks.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06713070720434189, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004767691250890493, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.0038974557537585497, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.00279864645563066, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0014918780652806163, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0012984111672267318, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0011582672595977783, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0005937344976700842, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0005398739012889564, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0005034790374338627, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5021320, 'end': 5056188}, 'sentences_idx_start': 489, 'sentences_idx_end': 493}, {'text': 'Yeah, totally great point. And ask a question now from Bert. So Bert says. Very impressive. Solving generative models with more generative models sounds very promising. What about replacing ants with convolutions? Talking about like a meta learning algorithm, like having a neural network that learns how to optimize other neural networks? Yeah, this concept, I think is introduced at some point in machine learning learn.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8735781908035278, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01572338491678238, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.01538635604083538, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.005699655972421169, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0024723538663238287, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007126887794584036, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00040991901187226176, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00032320377067662776, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0002832491009030491, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0002791100414469838, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5056354, 'end': 5094190}, 'sentences_idx_start': 494, 'sentences_idx_end': 501}, {'text': 'But we wanted to apply for nature based method that mimics like the Mother Nature, which is nature is the most efficient optimization evolution system. So looking at the results that are there in nature applying nature based methods they were superior to any other method. And the results we got also which just pointed that out that we saw good performance coming out from these results from our results and the previous results from other methods as well. Hop in here a little bit too.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05334658920764923, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.025933513417840004, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.02483660727739334, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.01670381799340248, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.008272415027022362, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0027508409693837166, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0015730649465695024, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.000634272932074964, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004828674718737602, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GreenSolutions'}, {'relevance': 0.0003088967932853848, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5094260, 'end': 5136140}, 'sentences_idx_start': 502, 'sentences_idx_end': 505}, {'text': "In the case of neural architecture search there's kind of a couple of classes of approaches. One is constructive, so kind of like where you build larger and larger networks and try and keep your network size minimal to try and find your optimal solution. Other types of neural architecture search approaches use like a superstructure and this is kind of how the earlier iterations of this were where you have a bound of your search space and you try and find the optimal network within that bound.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0222938135266304, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00405117915943265, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0038933854084461927, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0015917988494038582, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010446870001032948, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007240949780680239, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.000690932443831116, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0005970257334411144, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004549861478153616, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00016685185255482793, 'label': 'Education>PrivateSchool'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5137550, 'end': 5164354}, 'sentences_idx_start': 506, 'sentences_idx_end': 508}, {'text': "So one is like trying to build things from the ground up and the other one is trying to trim down a big network to a small network. As to your question about convolutions, there's been a fair bit of research lately in what's called graph based neural networks which can use convolutions over like a discrete graph search space and can potentially produce other graphs. And I believe there's been some neural architecture search work using this.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015255575999617577, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0076460447162389755, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.005342746619135141, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.004065786954015493, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0024272960145026445, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002360144630074501, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002120121382176876, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.001648810226470232, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014689882518723607, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003850777866318822, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5164402, 'end': 5193070}, 'sentences_idx_start': 509, 'sentences_idx_end': 511}, {'text': 'But one of the main and I think cool things about the approach here, which is different from those is if even if you have a graph based neural network and you have your search base defined as some kind of matrix where things are off and on depending on which nodes are connected to each other. You have a fixed search space which may not be big enough or it might not be the correct search space for this neural architecture search problem where this method here is all continuous. Right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3613360524177551, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.011720809154212475, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0051301936618983746, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020042096730321646, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.000953864713665098, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009474772377870977, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00040087333763949573, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00020668165234383196, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00019590002193581313, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00018270371947437525, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5193220, 'end': 5218854}, 'sentences_idx_start': 512, 'sentences_idx_end': 514}, {'text': "So within this continuous search space it gives the algorithm a lot of freedom, maybe too much freedom but a really open ended way of generating a wide variety of neural architectures which if you preconstrain your algorithm to work within a fixed discrete superstructure you may not even find them because they're not even a possibility. So that's one of the reasons we didn't go that route.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.048838578164577484, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007175631821155548, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006574269384145737, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00366212148219347, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002538413507863879, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0019283444853499532, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007858501048758626, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005323244258761406, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005045917350798845, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00043118963367305696, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5218892, 'end': 5246026}, 'sentences_idx_start': 515, 'sentences_idx_end': 516}, {'text': "But there are graph based neural architecture search algorithms out there where basically you take the architecture as a graph, you train a neural network to spit out another graph that it might think is better and those use convolutions. Sometimes that helps. That's awesome. So convolution sounds like yes.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05672316998243332, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.02040998823940754, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006707480177283287, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.003930582199245691, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.001059592585079372, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0009314470225945115, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00043618527706712484, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00034193595638498664, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00032285976340062916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00023443739337380975, 'label': 'Education>PrivateSchool'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5246058, 'end': 5266854}, 'sentences_idx_start': 517, 'sentences_idx_end': 520}, {'text': 'And one thought on that is yes, the ants solve all these incredible patterns and kind of do amazing things amidst informational and physical limitations like we all do having the ants be able to just make trade offs within a task space and then have a dial as modelers to make that task space. Kind of like touching the pheromone distribution or metacognitive ants or something emulating essentially that. And for example, the active inference forward looking and thinking through other minds that there could be a kind of cognitive colony.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.10473426431417465, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.023031732067465782, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.002453091088682413, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.002270044293254614, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0022089898120611906, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.0009472037781961262, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007778836297802627, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0006609632400795817, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0004873816214967519, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0004427389649208635, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5266972, 'end': 5323214}, 'sentences_idx_start': 521, 'sentences_idx_end': 523}, {'text': "So then that enables in silico total thought, experiment colonies and through data driven processes also kind of keep continuity with that model, perhaps literally continuity with the model and then connect it to empirical, which is something that is very hard for agent based modeling which, as you kind of pointed to, often sets certain fixed axes, performs like asweep looks at one mechanism, doesn't look at all these possible mechanisms of learning and intra and intergenerational and all these time effects.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.014635613188147545, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.01045189518481493, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.005263582803308964, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0044127875007689, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0030550749506801367, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016389272641390562, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0012635267339646816, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001180070685222745, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0011267042718827724, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006845655734650791, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5323362, 'end': 5366390}, 'sentences_idx_start': 524, 'sentences_idx_end': 524}, {'text': "So how do you see this being used in different research or application domains? Well, the main use case that we're thinking of was neural architecture search to apply it for other domains other than neural architecture. We didn't figure out that yet. I think Alex can explain on that. I can hop in a little bit mean.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.45473265647888184, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.029452072456479073, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.011400090530514717, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.009709764271974564, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.008754436857998371, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0065388125367462635, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006308865267783403, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.006062341388314962, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002388434950262308, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.002277786610648036, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5366890, 'end': 5402816}, 'sentences_idx_start': 525, 'sentences_idx_end': 529}, {'text': "So basically this type of algorithm, if you need to generate graphs and you don't necessarily have a fixed structure for that graph and when I say graph, I mean like a computer science graph where you have nodes in a different so pretty much anything involving graph construction. I think these types of methods work. Neural networks kind of under the hood can be represented as graphs and usually are.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.17441169917583466, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.13183428347110748, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.05412030965089798, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.009574305266141891, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.008588464930653572, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006403214298188686, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0026581452693790197, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0023254125844687223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007922499789856374, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.000755008717533201, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5402858, 'end': 5427536}, 'sentences_idx_start': 530, 'sentences_idx_end': 532}, {'text': "So I think we're using it for neural networks because it's really popular but there's other algorithms out there like the traditional traveling salesman, there's like routing problems, all that, any type of stuff where you might need to generate a graph in a smart way to do that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9014776349067688, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.03280019387602806, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.028413427993655205, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.017788227647542953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.012226443737745285, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.010044817812740803, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.009310008026659489, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.005811765789985657, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0034640522208064795, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.003201859537512064, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5427638, 'end': 5446230}, 'sentences_idx_start': 533, 'sentences_idx_end': 533}, {'text': "To your other point though, I think what's really cool here and I don't want to steal Alto Robin's thunder, but his last point on future direction is while a particular version of this ant colony optimization search is running to find an optimal neural network, a colony has fixed parameters that it operates within. But if you think of the colony as an organism as opposed to the ants being an organism, you can evolve colonies that optimize how the ants themselves act.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13241459429264069, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.043903104960918427, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005024290643632412, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002020579529926181, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009630527347326279, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0008192245149984956, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0005334767047315836, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00048738348414190114, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00045429469901137054, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00040041370084509254, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5446920, 'end': 5477168}, 'sentences_idx_start': 534, 'sentences_idx_end': 535}, {'text': "So you can have evolving colonies that in a smaller sense also evolve or optimize what they're doing within their prescripted parameters for the agents they're generating. So you can have like a meta meta. It's awesome. I mean the evolutionary account of a why question for ant behavior today, one part of that answer is like because colonies that couldn't under that regularity or constraint survive. We've had a long, long time to wipe those off the table.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7405152916908264, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.002693003509193659, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.002576093189418316, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0011587075423449278, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0011068402091041207, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009926060447469354, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.00021723410463891923, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00020440806110855192, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00019176342175342143, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00019168079597875476, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5477254, 'end': 5511924}, 'sentences_idx_start': 536, 'sentences_idx_end': 540}, {'text': 'And so every biological system has to have that kind of multiscale ordering. In 2021 we made the active imper ants paper which was modified from an epistemic foraging visual attention task about scanning around and then learning a cicade policy that had to do with epistemic foraging but not leaving a trace.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.4182490110397339, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.06014286354184151, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.003135619917884469, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.002727838698774576, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.002066392218694091, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0014521849807351828, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.0013148385332897305, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0008099662372842431, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007295005489140749, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0006854587118141353, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5512052, 'end': 5536460}, 'sentences_idx_start': 541, 'sentences_idx_end': 542}, {'text': "And then the main modification to bring that active inference epistemic visual foraging model into the active inference ant setting was to add a pheromone rule, just like you described, even though, of course, again, that's not the only pheromone rule, but that's just the most simple pheromone rule that we can generalize from, as you definitely have. And there are just many emerging ways of modeling those multiscale active inference models.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7692053914070129, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.05665932968258858, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0018702923553064466, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}, {'relevance': 0.0011097572278231382, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0006184463272802532, 'label': 'Sports>HuntingAndShooting'}, {'relevance': 0.0006126670050434768, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0005417614011093974, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.0004008978430647403, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ColdAndFlu'}, {'relevance': 0.00039164506597444415, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PersonalCelebrations&LifeEvents>Birth'}, {'relevance': 0.0003429120406508446, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5536540, 'end': 5561076}, 'sentences_idx_start': 543, 'sentences_idx_end': 544}, {'text': "So composing across layers, which we might associate more with the kind of laterality of things that happen through interactions. And then also, as Mike Levin shows, with kind of the time diamond systems that have a memory retention component of some shape, cognitive shape, and then a protention awareness or agency or other attributes you can use to describe that. And that's a statistically amenable way to describe things.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.16817879676818848, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.03660738840699196, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.011526426300406456, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01101061049848795, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0038418907206505537, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.003043547971174121, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002666405402123928, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002471768297255039, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.002030003583058715, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.001901061274111271, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5561108, 'end': 5597430}, 'sentences_idx_start': 545, 'sentences_idx_end': 547}, {'text': "And then there's a variety of implementations on a given statistical problem, or like Federated Compute architecture, it might be the case that you're not running the pure matrix multiplications that are shown in the early MATLAB code of active inference. Different components of machine learning systems might be kind of composed together, also ways kind of abiding by those patterns of communication. But then there's a level of abstraction that we can still describe, but it doesn't mean active inference is going to be kind of causing it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.18026773631572723, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.11069823801517487, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.08767661452293396, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.016247259452939034, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.008752856403589249, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0030524269677698612, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0016570409061387181, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010642283596098423, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010541882365942001, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006614165613427758, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5598440, 'end': 5633408}, 'sentences_idx_start': 548, 'sentences_idx_end': 550}, {'text': "So that's what gives a lot of flexibility. And it's really cool that through your background, Alexander and work and these kinds of collaborations that like the active inference perspective on multi agent modeling with all these other views can at least come together comparatively. And then that is going to, I think, be quite an interesting interchange to apply this entire tissue type or colony type thinking above and within the models. Just a lot of degrees of freedom, like you said, could be too.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.028606314212083817, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.012121597304940224, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.009178091771900654, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.002806315431371331, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016652739141136408, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0014027829747647047, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.0010018331231549382, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0009623983060009778, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005822278908453882, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0005773563752882183, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5633574, 'end': 5672510}, 'sentences_idx_start': 551, 'sentences_idx_end': 554}, {'text': "And I think there's different ways too, I think depends on how you want to take the ant metaphor. And again, it's kind of interesting, some of the questions or comments that you're making, Daniel, and some from the audience about how does this think about it from a cognitive point of view. I mean, I do work in cognitive architectures, of course, again, kind of from the whole single agent or single entity and modeling a single brain in its different regions.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1557241976261139, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.040590375661849976, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.004026526119560003, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0017419421346858144, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0013710773782804608, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011979948030784726, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}, {'relevance': 0.0007375329150818288, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005664922064170241, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004973128088749945, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0004933345480822027, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5673440, 'end': 5703940}, 'sentences_idx_start': 555, 'sentences_idx_end': 557}, {'text': "But I think if you take a nature inspired optimization approach like the ant metaphor that Abdel Rahman latched onto, and that's sort of like the way in which he formalizes how takes a principle of how ants interact with their world, interact with each other, and then mathematically model those particular concepts step by step. And I think if you bend the metaphor and say, well, okay, could the ant colony metaphor apply to multi human agent systems, right, or other entities?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.10573367774486542, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.018167871981859207, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.007870293222367764, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0037489840760827065, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0033456580713391304, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0025481560733169317, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002259527798742056, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0009642458171583712, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0008284974028356373, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006817835383117199, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5704020, 'end': 5741140}, 'sentences_idx_start': 558, 'sentences_idx_end': 559}, {'text': "Does the ant necessarily can it be generalized beyond the physical creature upon which Abdul Rahman based his initial metaphor? And that's an interesting philosophical kind of take to it. And then how do you apply that to, let's say, building a multi agent cognitive system.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.33403846621513367, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.16237005591392517, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.004094358999282122, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0036983343306928873, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0032082009129226208, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0026962098199874163, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.002228586934506893, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0011124967131763697, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0008195887203328311, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0007761982851661742, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5741960, 'end': 5760008}, 'sentences_idx_start': 560, 'sentences_idx_end': 562}, {'text': "And then, of course, as Travis was discussing with you and you were mentioning metacognition know, you could think of ant colonies, of ant colonies, but you could even replace the word ant and just say, well, we have clusters of intelligent agents, or whatever degree of modeling we're doing.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9863324761390686, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.025861410424113274, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.008112786337733269, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004741471726447344, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001954929204657674, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0014196045231074095, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.000823767448309809, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0008128335466608405, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0005308671970851719, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.0003739952517207712, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5760094, 'end': 5777452}, 'sentences_idx_start': 563, 'sentences_idx_end': 563}, {'text': "Because again, I do want to emphasize that at least the cans and ants agents that I have worked with in the context of the Raman, they are not each and of themselves, even, I would argue, if nothing else, a very extremely simplified generative model or a very simple control system. There's no neural network under each one because then you'd have to simulate computationally each one of these ants within the framework.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.44938603043556213, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.14166656136512756, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.10721314698457718, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0034092937130481005, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003383699571713805, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001121250563301146, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.001053070998750627, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0010002708295360208, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0009126124787144363, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0008265777141787112, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5777506, 'end': 5803444}, 'sentences_idx_start': 564, 'sentences_idx_end': 565}, {'text': "So I think there's always that practical machine learning kind of viewpoint of, well, there's always how do you simulate that? And Alderam is working with CPUs. It's not like he has an army of GPUs to replace them with convolutional networks. Again, if you had the resources, this would be awesome. But expense and money is another constraint on this planet.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9798968434333801, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.15754079818725586, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.09712208807468414, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008739965967833996, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.003785367589443922, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0035618185065686703, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.001411039032973349, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.000652673130389303, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0005449046147987247, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0005229934467934072, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5803492, 'end': 5824284}, 'sentences_idx_start': 566, 'sentences_idx_end': 570}, {'text': "But I think there's interesting views and interesting directions one could go by taking inspiration from the ant metaphor and the concept of pheromones and translate them to other real world signals and how, for example, communication patterns among other animal entities or other human agents. And I think that that opens up an interesting perspective.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11821989715099335, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.013156265020370483, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}, {'relevance': 0.00497620040550828, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Allergies'}, {'relevance': 0.0038004533853381872, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0028660125099122524, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.002813031431287527, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0026072468608617783, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>Menopause'}, {'relevance': 0.0019384281476959586, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0019250997574999928, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}, {'relevance': 0.0015523273032158613, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5824332, 'end': 5848368}, 'sentences_idx_start': 571, 'sentences_idx_end': 572}, {'text': "And if you're constantly trying to connect it back to free energy minimization and trying to say, well, how are we balancing the terms that you can decompose it into an epistemic and an instrumental, and how are these balancing out and how are these physical processes that we specify balancing those terms? That's just a very interesting place to be. And you mentioned active inference versions of Hans, and that's fascinating and of itself.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.579960823059082, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.4637603163719177, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002705598482862115, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0026564833242446184, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0016776920529082417, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0014422490494325757, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0012239126954227686, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0007463994552381337, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0007077667396515608, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0006822632276453078, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5848464, 'end': 5877216}, 'sentences_idx_start': 573, 'sentences_idx_end': 575}, {'text': "Last comment I have is, again, the degree of modeling and what you are modeling. Like, if you're modeling a society or organization, that's one way. You could use the ant colony framework, if you will, or metaheuristic optimization frameworks to then cast a system, any type of complex multi agent system, as an active inference kind of engaging process.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2995114028453827, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.031058581545948982, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.018920620903372765, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006847145967185497, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0035027842968702316, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.002720785792917013, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0018093918915838003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.001399453030899167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0012446934124454856, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009856190299615264, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5877398, 'end': 5904808}, 'sentences_idx_start': 576, 'sentences_idx_end': 578}, {'text': "Or you could go really low level and think about cells in a body or units that make up organs or organelles and trying to say, well, can we use this to model that level of granularity within, like a human or an animal entity? Right? And I think there's some fascinating questions about how does this metaphor manifest itself at different timescales and different degrees of perspective about how you're modeling? What are you looking at? What's the picture that you want to emulate?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9397907853126526, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.02319476380944252, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.01730600744485855, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.016058964654803276, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.009107924066483974, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002681232988834381, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.0016310991486534476, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0014599068090319633, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001180992810986936, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010709351627156138, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5904894, 'end': 5933244}, 'sentences_idx_start': 579, 'sentences_idx_end': 583}, {'text': "And of course, there's always under the hood, this practical consideration of, well, okay, the computational expense that you allocate, and are you able to actually run that simulation long enough? Because I think Abdul Rahman, you can correct me if I'm wrong. You mentioned one of the experiments I think was for the bigger systems took a month. Right. Of course this was on CPUs. That can get pretty prohibitive if you want to go even bigger than that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07997815310955048, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01642296276986599, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.008376194164156914, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004278494976460934, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Desktops'}, {'relevance': 0.004128527827560902, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011724584037438035, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0008974706870503724, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006744926213286817, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006307212170213461, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.000611481664236635, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5933292, 'end': 5959224}, 'sentences_idx_start': 584, 'sentences_idx_end': 589}, {'text': 'But again, I think it just depends on what hardware you have to simulate this on. Yeah. And also using high performance computing, it is not always feasible for smaller. So if we try to model the brain of Aims like small neural network, using a GPU might not be feasible solution. And Travis is a high performance computing specialist here, expert tell you that sending data to a GPU and getting it back is very time consuming and resources consuming.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.22962230443954468, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.18272490799427032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.04476252943277359, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.011754920706152916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017891566967591643, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010633168276399374, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0008666698704473674, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0007482853252440691, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0007251131464727223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006827793549746275, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5959262, 'end': 5992896}, 'sentences_idx_start': 590, 'sentences_idx_end': 594}, {'text': 'So it will worsen the time consumption rather than solving it, because communicating between the main memory and the GPU had an overhead. So it has to be a big enough problem to actually utilize this GPU in such solutions. Sorry, go ahead. When you have the super large language models, or large models for computer vision, they do a lot of just massive operations on Tensors, which are basically multidimensional matrices, right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2782338857650757, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.08091762661933899, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.03840011730790138, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.003671097569167614, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.003524258965626359, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0028124256059527397, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002455951413139701, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0017164209857583046, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015665539540350437, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0015198606997728348, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5992928, 'end': 6034384}, 'sentences_idx_start': 595, 'sentences_idx_end': 598}, {'text': 'And when you have really big wide Tensors, you can parallelize the operation really nicely across the GPU. A lot of this work is based on doing time series forecasting, time series classification on sensor data, stuff from like power systems. So the input to a large language model might be 1000 or more length of a word embedding, which is actually not huge. But if you go up to a computer vision model, the input image may be 1000 by 1000 pixels and that gives you actually a million inputs.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.36217001080513, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.15015433728694916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.01772591844201088, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.01558474451303482, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.01204573456197977, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.01015377789735794, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.008112635463476181, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.006788108963519335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.005402191076427698, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.005145634524524212, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6034502, 'end': 6071416}, 'sentences_idx_start': 599, 'sentences_idx_end': 602}, {'text': "Right. When you're working with sensor systems, off of aircraft, power plants, that type of thing, you may have 50 to 100 inputs. And when you're working with this type of time series data, you don't need a massive super wide neural network. And then if you add in recurrency where you have to do backprop over time and other things like this, you actually can't really parallelize it nicely on a GPU. So for us, the CPU is actually more efficient.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8455628156661987, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.06961910426616669, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.018679354339838028, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.013691131956875324, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007992250844836235, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.007300423923879862, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004101559054106474, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0036563286557793617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.003131442004814744, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001887829857878387, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6071448, 'end': 6093824}, 'sentences_idx_start': 603, 'sentences_idx_end': 607}, {'text': "We tried Abdul Rahman wrote a bunch of code a long time ago to put this stuff on GPUs and we found it was quite a bit slower. So, depending on what you're doing with a neural network, a GPU actually isn't the right answer.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08033490180969238, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.05022911727428436, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0019007690716534853, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014616589760407805, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013227943563833833, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009773471392691135, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006950330571271479, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0005374500178731978, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Desktops'}, {'relevance': 0.0005157118430361152, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00037027502548880875, 'label': 'Education>PrivateSchool'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6093872, 'end': 6104330}, 'sentences_idx_start': 608, 'sentences_idx_end': 609}, {'text': "But the other cool thing about this, which I think does have maybe even potential for there, is that one of the big not talked about problems in machine learning is that back propagation is the fastest thing we know, but it's inherently not scalable. You can get a bigger, better GPU to do your bits of your network in parallel to speed things up, but that only gets better if you have a bigger network.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.10250349342823029, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.013626335188746452, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.006612381897866726, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0062825181521475315, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00433078408241272, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.004082405008375645, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0012583372881636024, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0007531931041739881, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006455406546592712, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0006452454254031181, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6105180, 'end': 6129884}, 'sentences_idx_start': 610, 'sentences_idx_end': 611}, {'text': "If you want to speed up the training process, you can't just add another CPU or another GPU and make back prop go faster. You can make the forward and backward pass through your neural network faster. But you still have to do every epoch of backprop. Iteratively a method like this where we're generating one, it's backprop free. So it's not using backprop.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.037762757390737534, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0016885614022612572, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007091400329954922, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006811831262893975, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00021501007722690701, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00015112261462491006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00011917633673874661, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 8.996327960630879e-05, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 7.881337660364807e-05, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 7.369428931269795e-05, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6130012, 'end': 6152448}, 'sentences_idx_start': 612, 'sentences_idx_end': 616}, {'text': "We can use a nature inspired or other method to use hundreds of computers and you can throw twice as many computers at it and get a result twice as back, twice as fast, whereas backprop you can't do that. So if you think about actually being able to train a neural network backprop, actually it's got a pretty low speed limit for what we need to do.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7072357535362244, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.013998887501657009, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0032672241795808077, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002529703313484788, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002477854024618864, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.000323209329508245, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0002866105060093105, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00022692757192999125, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002255376020912081, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00011745694791898131, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6152624, 'end': 6173324}, 'sentences_idx_start': 617, 'sentences_idx_end': 618}, {'text': "And it's kind of a big problem with the machine learning community that people don't like to talk about because they're like oh, I'll just buy the next big Nvidia GPU and that'll do things faster. That's super interesting. Does this maybe even bring up a kind of relationship where things like a graphics visualization of course a GPU does well and that's like the screen changing through time with a classical process that can be massively unfolded.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.71568363904953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.2652718722820282, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.08740641921758652, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.022470995783805847, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.016949957236647606, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0064410497434437275, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.005390426144003868, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.00351715087890625, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0022