nding pathfinding sensor integration, polarization of light, like different cognitive strategies because they might be going out long distance and dragging something home, not leaving any pheromone because it's not any more likely to have food there.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5981134176254272, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0055973646230995655, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0024091547820717096, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0016209518071264029, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0016169077716767788, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0013139289803802967, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0012050201185047626, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0009558015153743327, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009207121911458671, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0008727836539037526, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6238624, 'end': 6275088}, 'sentences_idx_start': 628, 'sentences_idx_end': 630}, {'text': "So in that case, the stigma g is basically minimal to essentially none. And then in other situations you could have something that's very adherent to distributions to the point of being fit to a very kind of normative path. But that's happening at a level that allows the different compute architectures, different information architectures and ultimately different biological embodiments to really engage fruitfully. Again looking at the variability, the diversity of biological algorithms for collective behavior which have been studied by Professor Gordon and others in so many different angles.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07098452001810074, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.06788002699613571, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01402604952