ality>Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6389914, 'end': 6417896}, 'sentences_idx_start': 646, 'sentences_idx_end': 647}, {'text': "However, for full generality, at least to the space that we know of, biological life forms and their engagements and ecological engagements, not just like within one behavior, that space is so vast and there's so much to learn across different systems within two. Again, to abduce away into different information architectures and active inference being some subset or type of those. So it's awesome work. Do you have any last comments?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9776881337165833, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.798675000667572, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.34593459963798523, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.06633129715919495, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.008221065625548363, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.006543916184455156, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.004489187616854906, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0038350641261786222, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0026653658133000135, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.002443965757265687, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6418088, 'end': 6452920}, 'sentences_idx_start': 648, 'sentences_idx_end': 651}, {'text': 'Well, giving ability for brands to be self aware and aware about its environment is actually something that we implemented in our last work with the BP free camps. They are indirectly aware about their environment and they are adapting to the changes in their clinical environment by indirectly meaning that they are evolving using a genetic based algorithm to just change their behavior, like how they sense the hormones when they take the steps and some other times or some other characteristics they have.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8861764073371887, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.7735969424247742, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.5724300742149353, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AdvertisingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.19039766490459442, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityStyle'}, {'relevance': 0.008042692206799984, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.005759481340646744, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ConsumerIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.004337603691965342, 'label': 'Style&Fashion'}, {'relevance': 0.003707029391080141, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RetailIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0028824948240071535, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty>NaturalAndOrganicBeauty'}, {'relevance': 0.002872406505048275, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6457970, 'end': 6498026}, 'sentences_idx_start': 652, 'sentences_idx_end': 653}, {'text': "So they are adapting, but kind of like not in an intelligent way, but through evolution. If you want to say, actually, we considered putting a brain in each one of these agents. But then again, as Travis and Alex mentioned, we found that it won't be practical. Actually, it would hinder our Asynchronous design because we couldn't prolize that it will take time to train each one of these brains as we evolve the neural networks. Awesome. Alexander or Travis, any last thoughts?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9982518553733826, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.03228133171796799, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.011523020453751087, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0049002571031451225, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006415652460418642, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006189038977026939, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0003658063360489905, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0003466352354735136, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00032535422360524535, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0003081787726841867, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6498128, 'end': 6543760}, 'sentences_idx_start': 654, 'sentences_idx_end': 659}, {'text': "Okay, I'm just really happy. I mean, I think this work is really interesting and it opens up a lot of pretty cool avenues. Again, if we can get to the point where we're evolving colonies that are producing ants and can see where that can go. So one of the big issues in neural architecture search is the whole question of what is an optimal neural network and what an optimal neural network is. Could be different for what will be different for different tasks.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2665906846523285, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.04691481962800026, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.017532015219330788, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0026446597184985876, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.002174768364056945, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009704732801765203, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006754867499694228, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005343856755644083, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0004955914337188005, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00043231117888353765, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6552670, 'end': 6584514}, 'sentences_idx_start': 660, 'sentences_idx_end': 664}, {'text': "But not only that, even if it's the same data set, how you're using that neural network could lead to a lesser, more optimal neural network, right? Depending on what you're doing with it, maybe you need one that's more energy efficient. Maybe you don't care about energy efficiency or performance, and you'll take a slower neural network, but you need more accuracy.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04857446998357773, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001783594023436308, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010194319766014814, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006576762534677982, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0003667139681056142, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003478416765574366, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028290337650105357, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00015404664736706764, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00013547659909818321, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00013533340825233608, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6584562, 'end': 6603174}, 'sentences_idx_start': 665, 'sentences_idx_end': 667}, {'text': "So being able to have algorithms which can automate this whole process for us and tune them to what we actually want to use the neural network for is really important. And I think, one, just having ant colony optimization be able to optimize a network for a problem is great. But two, if we can make it such that the algorithm itself is self optimizing, it really can streamline this whole process where right now, if you're doing machine learning, it can be kind of miserable.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6756588816642761, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.06902685016393661, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.025608349591493607, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.006186367478221655, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003673233324661851, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0035031402949243784, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0013199193635955453, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010972128948196769, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0009387835743837059, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005936212837696075, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6603302, 'end': 6629454}, 'sentences_idx_start': 668, 'sentences_idx_end': 670}, {'text': "You make a neural network architecture, you try it out, see how well it does. Oh no, that didn't do so well. Let me tweak a couple of knobs automating that process. My whole life as a computer scientist is about being lazy, but being smart about it. So whatever I can optimize so that I don't have to do it over and over again seems like a good use of my time.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9884880185127258, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.3944424092769623, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.09393250197172165, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0660363957285881, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002231004647910595, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.001091001438908279, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0010219840332865715, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0009584789513610303, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0009581958875060081, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0004883233341388404, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6629502, 'end': 6651450}, 'sentences_idx_start': 671, 'sentences_idx_end': 675}, {'text': "So I'll be smart about having to do as little as possible in the future. I don't have too much to add to that. I think a lot of the good discussion has happened already, and we talked about various implications and ways of viewing ant colony optimization from other perspectives, including an active inference point of view.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6688859462738037, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0011794627644121647, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0008303674403578043, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0006373412325046957, 'label': 'Pets>FishAndAquariums'}, {'relevance': 0.0005779849016107619, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.00042116278200410306, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>Vaccines'}, {'relevance': 0.00040512013947591186, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.000360011646989733, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00032939473749138415, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AviationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003081211762037128, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>AntivirusSoftware'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6651520, 'end': 6676210}, 'sentences_idx_start': 676, 'sentences_idx_end': 678}, {'text': "So I guess really more from a closing thought on my end, is that it will be interesting, or it is an interesting direction to think about, like I said earlier or suggested, about the adaptation of the metaphor to other systems. And what are you trying to model and what's your goals from a scientific and philosophical point of view? What are questions you seek to answer? And I think it might be very interesting, again, given other developments and computing technology and ways in which you implement.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8162966370582581, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.6731900572776794, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.24777257442474365, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.10223370045423508, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.023705242201685905, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.017794452607631683, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0051220497116446495, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.004463160410523415, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004244278650730848, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0030486667528748512, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6676360, 'end': 6711498}, 'sentences_idx_start': 679, 'sentences_idx_end': 682}, {'text': "The parallelization that, I think, is that's what attracted me the most to a lot of these meta heuristic algorithms, even things like particle swarm. And when I worked with Travis many years ago on the exam algorithms, you saw our names on that and working on that type of stuff.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.012900158762931824, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003257683478295803, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.002512723905965686, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002136219060048461, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.001052198582328856, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006563637871295214, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0005819743382744491, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005483488203026354, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00041253413655795157, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00029866350814700127, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6711674, 'end': 6730102}, 'sentences_idx_start': 683, 'sentences_idx_end': 684}, {'text': 'The part that always caught my attention is, again, that ability to say, I can put these entities on different processing, computing, processing resources or devices, and then they will interact and exchange their results in some way to try to optimize some often complex multi objective cost function.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.44758349657058716, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.4374386966228485, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.36022937297821045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.08224046230316162, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.057133518159389496, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.03682835027575493, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006488272920250893, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005312580149620771, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004093234892934561, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.003741207765415311, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6730156, 'end': 6751658}, 'sentences_idx_start': 685, 'sentences_idx_end': 685}, {'text': "And so I think the part that we'll see or that would encourage the wider spread adoption of even like meta heuristic algorithms in general, not to say that they aren't used a lot in, for example, the engineering domains is again the development of parallel computing processing systems and I think exploiting things like asynchronous computing. That was again another angle that caught my attention from Travis. He's done a lot of work on genetic optimization and neurovolution from an asynchronous point of view.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8752059936523438, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.325646311044693, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.09685055166482925, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.026255115866661072, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.006804691627621651, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0036733464803546667, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015217156615108252, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0009764973074197769, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007403376512229443, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007322870078496635, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6751744, 'end': 6781622}, 'sentences_idx_start': 686, 'sentences_idx_end': 688}, {'text': "And how can we allocate, whatever resources are available and distributing them across global networks? I think that might be the best shot to scaling up, let's say, with what we got right now. There might be again, you've mentioned, Daniel, quantum technology. Quantum computing is another interesting place that sort of like changes the barring technologies that we don't necessarily have exactly at their best at this moment.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9375120997428894, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.2788574695587158, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.1982923001050949, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.17164449393749237, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.08273325115442276, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.017176548019051552, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet'}, {'relevance': 0.011683182790875435, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.009318733587861061, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.006009130273014307, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>InternetServiceProviders'}, {'relevance': 0.004737998824566603, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebHosting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6781676, 'end': 6811038}, 'sentences_idx_start': 689, 'sentences_idx_end': 692}, {'text': "How can we take advantage of citizen science or distributed computing or peer to peer type of communication and building massive active inference systems that embody like the multi agent metaphor of ant colony optimization or other nature inspired frameworks? And can this system evolve over very long spans of time, just like evolution really worked? Another piece, my final comp and is that why I'm interested sometimes in evolution is that to me it is the inductive bias that provided us with structures that allow, for example, a human agent.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9257423877716064, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.29478219151496887, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.18646761775016785, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.14247038960456848, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.015048593282699585, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.005922814831137657, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.005006114020943642, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.003363431664183736, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.002167205326259136, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0018181881168857217, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6811204, 'end': 6852794}, 'sentences_idx_start': 693, 'sentences_idx_end': 695}, {'text': 'Babies can to operate already. Babies can already recognize faces, right? And we have certain instinctual reactions and certain mechanisms that evolution has endowed us with. And so a fascinating question is what is the interplay of the idea of simulating an artificial form of evolution? Maybe building DNA structures or very simplified computational structures?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6159924268722534, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.1225554421544075, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.1156395822763443, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.10589658468961716, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.055058516561985016, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting'}, {'relevance': 0.024460457265377045, 'label': "Shopping>Children'sGamesAndToys"}, {'relevance': 0.012458033859729767, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.008485251106321812, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ModelToys'}, {'relevance': 0.0077316490933299065, 'label': 'Education>EarlyChildhoodEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.004968326073139906, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6852912, 'end': 6877246}, 'sentences_idx_start': 696, 'sentences_idx_end': 700}, {'text': "Which would answer Abdel Rahman's concern about, well, maybe we don't want the agents to be too smart in of themselves because I can't really simulate that unless you give me like a decade to run the simulator. But you could maybe come up with a more fundamental primitive and then use that as a starting point for your neural network. Let's say, Daniel, you want to do some task in image segmentation and like okay, but what can your evolutionary framework give me?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9993140697479248, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.032652243971824646, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.03179655596613884, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.007233465556055307, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0027015937957912683, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0011149010388180614, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0010199997341260314, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004482038493733853, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00037569619598798454, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00036471104249358177, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6877278, 'end': 6903002}, 'sentences_idx_start': 701, 'sentences_idx_end': 703}, {'text': "Well, I'll say here here's a template to start from. This is a kernel on which you build your framework and it's like a DNA structure. And this has evolved across many years of distributed peer to peer computing. And you could imagine building this mammoth evolving, continual learning style evolutionary algorithm, whether it is based on genetic algorithms or ant colony. And you could imagine that might be an interesting way to think about.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.20040912926197052, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.1352112889289856, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.019816897809505463, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01851106435060501, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005747888702899218, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.005278183612972498, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.004343018867075443, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0030920852441340685, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00276154070161283, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.002726770006120205, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 6903056, 'end': 6932262}, 'sentences_idx_start': 704, 'sentences_idx_end': 708}, {'text': "And by the way, I am spitballing and generating an idea of how I could envision a scalable form without inventing a new computing system that I don't know will or will not exist because quantum has a lot of problems still to solve too, like superconducting or super temperatures or trapping photons, as I have learned. So that might be an interesting direction. I think the scaling of this, especially from the practical end, is going to be the most important. We're going to.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11535504460334778, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.06572162359952927, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.03126596286892891, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.007267042528837919, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.004222036339342594, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0032015275210142136, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0026963583659380674, 'label': 