': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'like', 'start': 6088278, 'end': 6088416, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'this,', 'start': 6088438, 'end': 6088576, 'confidence': 0.99999, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'you', 'start': 6088598, 'end': 6088736, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'actually', 'start': 6088758, 'end': 6088944, 'confidence': 0.99998, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': "can't", 'start': 6088982, 'end': 6089196, 'confidence': 0.99994, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'really', 'start': 6089228, 'end': 6089376, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'parallelize', 'start': 6089398, 'end': 6089996, 'confidence': 0.44846, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'it', 'start': 6090028, 'end': 6090176, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'nicely', 'start': 6090198, 'end': 6090476, 'confidence': 0.99997, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'on', 'start': 6090508, 'end': 6090608, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 6090614, 'end': 6090688, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'GPU.', 'start': 6090694, 'end': 6091272, 'confidence': 0.9995, 'speaker': 'C'}]}, {'text': "So for us, the CPU is actually more efficient. We tried Abdul Rahman wrote a bunch of code a long time ago to put this stuff on GPUs and we found it was quite a bit slower. So, depending on what you're doing with a neural network, a GPU actually isn't the right answer. But the other cool thing about this, which I think does have maybe even potential for there, is that one of the big not talked about problems in machine learning is that back propagation is the fastest thing we know, but it's inherently not scalable. You can get a bigger, better GPU to do your bits of your network in parallel to speed things up, but that only gets better if you have a bigger network.", 'start': 6091356, 'end': 6129884, 'confidence': 0.9908, 'words': [{'text': 'So', 'start': 6091356, 'end': 6091700, 'confidence': 0.9908, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'for', 'start': 6091770, 'end': 6091956,